  <event id="10">
      <start>12:00</start>
      <duration>01:00</duration>
      <room>H.2214</room>
      <slug></slug>
      <title>RPM Packaging</title>
      <subtitle></subtitle>
      <track>CentOS + Fedora</track>
      <type></type>
      <language></language>
      <abstract>&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Increasingly, managing collections of package metadata is more important than building packages. This presentation proposes several possible implementations in RPM development that may simplify creating collections.&#xA;&lt;/p&gt;&#xA; </abstract>
      <description>&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Several RPM development topics will be discussed: &#xA;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;ul&gt;&lt;li&gt; using easily extracted XML or YAML markup to represent metadata in *.rpm packages. &#xA;&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt; generating Provides: dependencies during install, not during build. &#xA;&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt; adding user-definable extensible tags to rpm metadata. &#xA;&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt; automating package scriptlet actions through rule based triggers.&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;/ul&gt;&#xA; </description>
      <persons>
          <person id="101">Jeff Johnson</person>
      </persons>
      <links></links>
      <video></video>
      <end></end>
  </event>